      note: Every Joern JVM is pinned to the 21 JDK by the provisioned wrapper, which is why the two JDKs are assessed separately.

    decisive measured fact:
      The two JDKs in this harness come from different release cycles. The build JDK reports 'openjdk version "17.0.20" 2026-07-21' -- the July original. The Joern JDK reports 'openjdk version "21.0.12.1" 2026-08-18 LTS' -- an August '.1' respin. So the harness already contains a respun JDK on one stream and the un-respun original on the other; the 17 stream's respin exists and was simply not the build this host was provisioned with.

