  what a human must do
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    At provisioning, replace /opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-17.0.20+8 with jdk-17.0.20.1+1 and update the AAP 0.4.1 Adoptium row and the environment record together, so the pin and the disk agree at all times -- the failure mode SEC-02 demonstrates for the graph is the same failure mode a half-applied JDK swap would create here. Then rebuild the pinned Spark reactor and rebuild the graph, because a JDK change changes the bytecode the frontend reads and therefore every graph count. Do not swap the JDK without rebuilding: a dataset whose bytecode was produced by one JDK and whose record names another is the class of contradiction this checkpoint already halts on.

